x667 text "Views and edits"
x668 puts x666 x667
x669 call close x668 
x670 call open x669 2
x671 write x670 2
x672 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
